$ jailops app info postgresql
App postgresql: PostgreSQL
  Summary:    Relational database server, PostgreSQL 18 from the FreeBSD packages.
  Category:   database
  License:    PostgreSQL
  Homepage:   https://www.postgresql.org/
  Image:      FreeBSD 15.1 or later, thin jail
  File:       postgresql.yaml (sha256:<sha256>)
  Source:     catalog

Description
  PostgreSQL is a relational database with transactions, replication and extensions.

  The cluster listens on localhost only until changed.

Packages
  postgresql18-server  ports  18.6

Services
  postgresql  started after the installation  rc.conf: postgresql_enable=YES

Ports
  NAME      PORT      EXPOSED  DESCRIPTION
  postgres  5432/tcp  no       The SQL port.

Data
  /var/db/postgres  The cluster (data18).

Configuration
  /var/db/postgres/data18/postgresql.conf  restart postgresql  Server settings.
  /var/db/postgres/data18/pg_hba.conf      restart postgresql  Who may connect.

Logs
  server  /var/log/messages  The port logs to syslog.

Setup
  /usr/sbin/chown postgres:postgres /var/db/postgres
  /usr/sbin/service postgresql initdb

Health
  /usr/local/bin/pg_isready -U postgres exits 0, within 60s

Access
  postgresql: jailops app allow makes a role and a database per grant and a line in /var/db/postgres/data18/pg_hba.conf (port postgres, service postgresql)

Resources
  memory 1G, disk 10G, cpu 1 (hints, not limits)

Notes
  Connect from inside the jail with: jailops exec NAME -- su -l postgres -c psql

$ jailops app info nginx -o yaml
definition:
  version: 1
  name: nginx
  title: nginx
  summary: Web server and reverse proxy, serving /usr/local/www.
  description: nginx is a small, fast web server and reverse proxy.
  category: web
  homepage: https://nginx.org/
  license: BSD-2-Clause
  image:
    os: freebsd
    release_min: "15.1"
  packages:
    - name: nginx
      repo: ports
      version: 1.30.6,3
  services:
    - name: nginx
      start: true
  ports:
    - name: http
      port: 80
      proto: tcp
      description: HTTP, the default site.
      expose: true
  data:
    - path: /usr/local/www
      description: The sites.
  config:
    - path: /usr/local/etc/nginx/nginx.conf
      description: The server configuration.
      restart: nginx
  logs:
    - name: access
      path: /var/log/nginx/access.log
      description: One line per request.
    - name: error
      path: /var/log/nginx/error.log
  health:
    http:
      port: 80
      path: /
      status: 200
    wait_seconds: 30
  resources:
    memory: 256M
    disk: 2G
    cpu: "1"
  notes: Put the site under /usr/local/www.
hash: sha256:<sha256>
file: nginx.yaml
source: catalog

